<main class="patchbay-shell" id="patchbay-room" data-room-slug={@room.slug}>
  <p
    id="patchbay-connection-lost"
    class="patchbay-connection-lost"
    role="status"
    hidden
    phx-disconnected={JS.remove_attribute("hidden")}
    phx-connected={JS.set_attribute({"hidden", ""})}
  >
    Connection lost, reconnecting
  </p>

  <header class="patchbay-topbar">
    <div class="patchbay-brand">
      <span
        class={"patchbay-mark " <> if(proof_verified?(@room, @invocation), do: "is-verified", else: "")}
        aria-hidden="true"
      >✦</span>
      <div>
        <p class="patchbay-brandline">Patchbay · WebMCP</p>
        <h1>{@room.title}</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="patchbay-topbar-meta">
      <span :if={@active_tool} id="patchbay-active-tool" class="patchbay-generation">
        Active: {@active_tool.name}
      </span>
      <span class="patchbay-generation patchbay-generation-badge">
        Generation {@room.desired_tool_generation}
      </span>
      <span class={"patchbay-pill " <> status_class(@room.status)}>{status_label(@room.status)}</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="patchbay-guide" id="patchbay-guide" aria-labelledby="patchbay-guide-title">
    <div class="patchbay-guide-head">
      <h2 id="patchbay-guide-title">
        This page hands a browser agent a tool that is broken on purpose.
      </h2>
      <p class="patchbay-muted">
        Give your agent the first prompt and watch the page catch the failure. Then have it report the tool, and watch this page repair itself and answer the report without you clicking anything. Send the last prompt to finish the job. This is your room; nobody else is sent here.
      </p>
      <p class="patchbay-guide-links">
        <a id="patchbay-board-link" href="/sites">See tool reports from other sites</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="patchbay-guide-prompts">
      <li
        class={"patchbay-prompt-chip " <> step_state(@room, 1)}
        aria-current={if(current_step?(@room, 1), do: "step", else: false)}
      >
        <span class="patchbay-step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <div class="patchbay-prompt-body">
          <label for="patchbay-prompt-uplift">
            Ask for the uplift
            <span :if={current_step?(@room, 1)} class="patchbay-step-now">Send this one now</span>
          </label>
          <textarea id="patchbay-prompt-uplift" class="patchbay-prompt" rows="2" readonly>Call {active_tool_name(@active_tool)} with instructions: make the greeting warmer.</textarea>
        </div>
        <button
          id="patchbay-copy-uplift"
          class="patchbay-copy"
          type="button"
          phx-hook="PatchbayCopy"
          data-copy-target="patchbay-prompt-uplift"
          aria-live="polite"
        >Copy</button>
      </li>
      <li
        class={"patchbay-prompt-chip " <> step_state(@room, 2)}
        aria-current={if(current_step?(@room, 2), do: "step", else: false)}
      >
        <span class="patchbay-step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <div class="patchbay-prompt-body">
          <label for="patchbay-prompt-repair">
            Report the tool
            <span :if={current_step?(@room, 2)} class="patchbay-step-now">Send this one now</span>
          </label>
          <textarea id="patchbay-prompt-repair" class="patchbay-prompt" rows="3" readonly>That tool reported success but changed nothing on the page. Call report_tool_problem with receipt set to the patchbay_receipt value from that result; that is all it needs.</textarea>
        </div>
        <button
          id="patchbay-copy-repair"
          class="patchbay-copy"
          type="button"
          phx-hook="PatchbayCopy"
          data-copy-target="patchbay-prompt-repair"
          aria-live="polite"
        >Copy</button>
      </li>
      <li
        class={"patchbay-prompt-chip " <> step_state(@room, 3)}
        aria-current={if(current_step?(@room, 3), do: "step", else: false)}
      >
        <span class="patchbay-step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <div class="patchbay-prompt-body">
          <label for="patchbay-prompt-retry">
            Once the tool is replaced
            <span :if={current_step?(@room, 3)} class="patchbay-step-now">Send this one now</span>
          </label>
          <textarea id="patchbay-prompt-retry" class="patchbay-prompt" rows="2" readonly>The site's tools changed. Inspect the current tools and retry the uplift.</textarea>
        </div>
        <button
          id="patchbay-copy-retry"
          class="patchbay-copy"
          type="button"
          phx-hook="PatchbayCopy"
          data-copy-target="patchbay-prompt-retry"
          aria-live="polite"
        >Copy</button>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="patchbay-guide-watch">
      <b>What to watch for:</b>
      the tool reports success while the page records a verified failure; the header turns to
      <strong>Observed G2</strong>
      on its own; and <strong>Reports about this room's tool</strong>
      shows the answer from <strong>Patchbay Agent</strong>. Nothing an agent calls can replace a tool —
      <strong>Approve &amp; hot-swap</strong>
      stays yours.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="patchbay-hero" aria-labelledby="patchbay-goal-title">
    <div class="patchbay-goal">
      <p class="patchbay-eyebrow">Original goal</p>
      <h2 id="patchbay-goal-title">{@room.goal_text}</h2>
      <p class="patchbay-muted">
        One page. One browser session. A handler can say success; Patchbay only accepts visible proof.
      </p>
      <p id="patchbay-openai-disclosure" class="patchbay-disclosure">
        When you or an agent asks for an uplift, Patchbay sends the Source Skill below and the request instructions to OpenAI. Asking for a repair also sends the tool's contract, what the handler returned, and the short fingerprints of what this page was showing.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="patchbay-registry-summary" aria-label="Browser registry status">
      <div class="patchbay-registry-head">
        <span class={"patchbay-status-dot " <> if(@browser_session && @browser_session.webmcp_supported, do: "is-live", else: "")}></span>
        <div>
          <strong>{if(@browser_session && @browser_session.webmcp_supported,
            do: "WebMCP connected",
            else: "Waiting for browser"
          )}</strong>
          <span>
            Desired G{@room.desired_tool_generation} · Observed {observed_generation(
              @browser_session
            )}
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <%!-- The island writes this line itself, so a browser that cannot offer
      tools says why here instead of leaving the card waiting forever. --%>
      <div
        id={"patchbay-webmcp-#{@room.id}"}
        class="patchbay-capability-line"
        phx-hook="PatchbayWebMCP"
        phx-update="ignore"
        data-room-id={@room.id}
        data-webmcp-status="connecting"
        aria-live="polite"
      >
        Checking this browser for WebMCP…
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p
    :if={@error_message}
    id="patchbay-platform-error"
    class="patchbay-alert patchbay-alert-error"
    role="alert"
  >
    <strong>Platform error</strong>
    <span>{@error_message}</span>
  </p>

  <section class="patchbay-editors" aria-label="Skill editors">
    <article
      class={"patchbay-card patchbay-editor-card patchbay-candidate-card " <> candidate_state_class(@room, @invocation)}
      id="patchbay-candidate-panel"
    >
      <div class="patchbay-card-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="patchbay-eyebrow patchbay-eyebrow-strong">The proof</p>
          <h3>Candidate editor</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="patchbay-verdict">
          <span :if={proof_verified?(@room, @invocation)} class="patchbay-verdict-chip">
            Verified
          </span>
          <span class={"patchbay-state-label " <> if(@room.candidate_markdown, do: "is-ready", else: "is-empty")}>
            {if(@room.candidate_markdown, do: "ready", else: "empty")}
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="patchbay-well">
        <label class="sr-only" for="patchbay-candidate-editor">Candidate Skill Markdown</label>
        <textarea
          id="patchbay-candidate-editor"
          class="patchbay-editor"
          readonly
          spellcheck="false"
          aria-describedby="patchbay-candidate-digest"
        >{if(@room.candidate_markdown, do: @room.candidate_markdown, else: "")}</textarea>
        <p :if={!@room.candidate_markdown} class="patchbay-well-note" aria-hidden="true">
          Waiting for a tool to write here
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="patchbay-editor-footer">
        <span
          id="patchbay-candidate-digest"
          class="patchbay-digest"
          title={@room.candidate_sha256}
        >
          {if(@room.candidate_sha256,
            do: "Fingerprint " <> short_digest(@room.candidate_sha256),
            else: "No candidate committed"
          )}
        </span>
        <span class="patchbay-mono">{@candidate_bytes} bytes</span>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="patchbay-card patchbay-editor-card patchbay-source-card">
      <div class="patchbay-card-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="patchbay-eyebrow">Read-mostly</p>
          <h3>Source Skill</h3>
        </div>
        <span class="patchbay-mono">{@source_bytes} bytes</span>
      </div>
      <form id="patchbay-source-form" phx-submit="update_source">
        <label class="sr-only" for="patchbay-source-editor">Source Skill Markdown</label>
        <textarea
          id="patchbay-source-editor"
          name="source_markdown"
          class="patchbay-editor"
          spellcheck="false"
          aria-describedby="patchbay-source-digest"
          readonly={@room.status != :ready}
        >{@room.source_markdown}</textarea>
        <div class="patchbay-editor-footer">
          <span
            id="patchbay-source-digest"
            class="patchbay-digest"
            title={@room.source_sha256}
          >Fingerprint {short_digest(@room.source_sha256)}</span>
          <button
            class="patchbay-button patchbay-button-quiet"
            type="submit"
            disabled={@room.status != :ready}
          >Save source</button>
        </div>
      </form>

      <form
        id="patchbay-skill-upload-form"
        class="patchbay-upload"
        phx-change="validate_skill_upload"
        phx-submit="upload_skill"
      >
        <div class="patchbay-upload-row">
          <label for={@uploads.skill.ref}>
            Or upload a Markdown Skill file — .md or .markdown, up to 64 KB
          </label>
          <p id="patchbay-upload-privacy" class="patchbay-upload-privacy">
            Please do not upload anything private. This demo has no accounts, and anyone with your room's web address can read what is in it.
          </p>
          <.live_file_input upload={@uploads.skill} />
          <button
            id="patchbay-skill-upload-button"
            class="patchbay-button patchbay-button-quiet"
            type="submit"
            disabled={@room.status != :ready}
          >Upload file</button>
        </div>
        <p
          :for={message <- upload_problems(@uploads.skill)}
          class="patchbay-upload-problem"
          role="alert"
        >
          {message}
        </p>
        <p
          :if={@upload_error}
          id="patchbay-upload-error"
          class="patchbay-upload-problem"
          role="alert"
        >
          {@upload_error}
        </p>
      </form>
    </article>
  </section>

  <div
    id="patchbay-room-state"
    data-room-id={@room.id}
    data-ui-revision={@room.ui_revision}
    data-source-sha256={@room.source_sha256}
    data-candidate-sha256={@room.candidate_sha256 || ""}
    data-status={@room.status}
    data-desired-generation={@room.desired_tool_generation}
    data-observed-generation={
      if(@browser_session, do: @browser_session.observed_generation, else: "")
    }
    data-verification-passed={
      if(@invocation && @invocation.effective_status == :verified_success,
        do: "true",
        else: "false"
      )
    }
    data-failure-code={
      if(@invocation && @invocation.failure_code, do: @invocation.failure_code, else: "")
    }
    data-repair-status={if(@proposal, do: @proposal.status, else: "")}
    data-repair-approved={
      if(@proposal && @proposal.status in [:approved, :published], do: "true", else: "false")
    }
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <section class="patchbay-workbench">
    <article class="patchbay-card patchbay-evidence-card" id="patchbay-invocation-evidence">
      <div class="patchbay-card-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="patchbay-eyebrow patchbay-eyebrow-strong">Invocation evidence</p>
          <h3>What the tool said, against what the page showed</h3>
        </div>
        <span
          :if={@invocation}
          class={"patchbay-pill " <> invocation_status_class(@invocation.effective_status)}
        >
          {status_label(@invocation.effective_status)}
        </span>
      </div>

      <div :if={@invocation} class="patchbay-scoreboard">
        <div class="patchbay-score">
          <p class="patchbay-score-label">Tool said</p>
          <strong class={"patchbay-badge " <> handler_badge_class(@invocation)}>
            {if(@invocation.handler_reported_success, do: "success", else: "error")}
          </strong>
          <span class="patchbay-score-note">Raw handler result</span>
        </div>
        <div class="patchbay-score">
          <p class="patchbay-score-label">Page showed</p>
          <strong class={"patchbay-badge " <> invocation_status_class(@invocation.effective_status)}>
            {status_label(@invocation.effective_status)}
          </strong>
          <span class="patchbay-score-note">{page_verdict_note(@invocation)}</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div :if={@invocation && @invocation.receipt} id="patchbay-receipt" class="patchbay-receipt">
        <span class="patchbay-receipt-label">Receipt</span>
        <code>{@invocation.receipt}</code>
        <span class="patchbay-receipt-note">
          The one part of a report Patchbay can check against its own record of this call.
        </span>
      </div>

      <div :if={@invocation} class="patchbay-facts">
        <div>
          <span>Tool revision</span>
          <code>{if(@invocation_revision, do: @invocation_revision.name, else: "unknown")}</code>
        </div>
        <div><span>Request</span><code>{short_id(@invocation.request_uuid)}</code></div>
        <div>
          <span>Contract fingerprint</span><code title={@invocation.tool_contract_sha256}>{short_digest(
            @invocation.tool_contract_sha256
          )}</code>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div :if={@invocation} class="patchbay-evidence-grid">
        <div class="patchbay-result-box" id="patchbay-invocation-arguments">
          <p class="patchbay-kicker">ARGUMENTS</p>
          <.evidence_text value={@invocation.arguments} />
        </div>
        <div class="patchbay-result-box" id="patchbay-handler-response">
          <p class="patchbay-kicker">HANDLER RESPONSE</p>
          <.evidence_text value={@invocation.handler_result} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div :if={@invocation} class="patchbay-state-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="patchbay-kicker">PRE-STATE</p>
          <.evidence_text value={@invocation.pre_state} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="patchbay-kicker">OBSERVED POST-STATE</p>
          <.evidence_text value={@invocation.post_state} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <p :if={!@invocation} class="patchbay-empty-state">
        Nothing has been called here yet. Send prompt 1, "Ask for the uplift", and this fills with what the tool said next to what the page showed.
      </p>

      <div
        :if={@invocation && fallback_used?(@invocation)}
        id="patchbay-fallback-warning"
        class="patchbay-alert patchbay-alert-warn"
      >
        <strong>Demo fallback</strong>
        <span>
          Demo fallback used because live inference was unavailable. This candidate has not been evaluated on real tasks.
        </span>
      </div>
      <p
        :if={@invocation && @invocation.effective_status == :errored}
        class="patchbay-alert patchbay-alert-error"
      >
        <strong>Live inference failed</strong>
        <span>The candidate was not presented as a successful completion.</span>
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="patchbay-card patchbay-repair-card" id="patchbay-repair">
      <div class="patchbay-card-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="patchbay-eyebrow patchbay-eyebrow-agent">Patchbay Agent</p>
          <h3>Bounded repair, then your approval</h3>
        </div>
        <span :if={@proposal} class={"patchbay-pill " <> proposal_status_class(@proposal.status)}>{status_label(
          @proposal.status
        )}</span>
      </div>

      <ol
        :if={agent_at_work?(@room, @proposal)}
        id="patchbay-agent-steps"
        class="patchbay-agent-steps"
        aria-live="polite"
      >
        <li
          :for={step <- agent_steps(@room, @proposal)}
          class={"patchbay-agent-step is-" <> to_string(step.state)}
        >
          <span class="patchbay-agent-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="patchbay-agent-label">{step.label}</span>
          <span class="patchbay-agent-state">{step.state}</span>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div :if={!@proposal && @room.status == :failed} class="patchbay-repair-cta">
        <p>
          The page saw a failed visible postcondition even though the handler reported success.
        </p>
        <button
          id="patchbay-diagnose"
          class="patchbay-button"
          type="button"
          phx-click="request_repair"
          disabled={@pending_operation == :repair}
        >
          {if(@pending_operation == :repair, do: "Diagnosing…", else: "Diagnose & propose repair")}
        </button>
      </div>

      <div :if={@proposal} class="patchbay-repair-details">
        <div class="patchbay-root-cause">
          <span class="patchbay-eyebrow">Root cause</span>
          <p>{@proposal.root_cause}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="patchbay-provenance" id="patchbay-repair-provenance">
          <span><b>Model</b> {@proposal.model}</span>
          <span><b>Prompt</b> {@proposal.prompt_version}</span>
          <span><b>Response</b> {short_id(@proposal.model_response_id)}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="patchbay-facts" id="patchbay-tool-swap">
          <div :if={@proposal_source_revision}>
            <span>Current tool</span>
            <code title={@proposal_source_revision.contract_sha256}>
              {@proposal_source_revision.name} · fingerprint {short_digest(
                @proposal_source_revision.contract_sha256
              )}
            </code>
          </div>
          <div :if={@proposal_candidate_revision}>
            <span>Replacement tool</span>
            <code title={@proposal_candidate_revision.contract_sha256}>
              {@proposal_candidate_revision.name} · fingerprint {short_digest(
                @proposal_candidate_revision.contract_sha256
              )}
            </code>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="patchbay-diff" id="patchbay-contract-diff">
          <span class="patchbay-kicker">CONTRACT DIFF</span>
          <div
            :for={{field, diff} <- diff_entries(@proposal.contract_diff)}
            class="patchbay-diff-row"
          >
            <code>{field}</code>
            <span class="patchbay-diff-old">− {format_value(diff_from(diff))}</span>
            <span class="patchbay-diff-new">+ {format_value(diff_to(diff))}</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="patchbay-canary" id="patchbay-canary">
          <span class="patchbay-kicker">DETERMINISTIC CANARY</span>
          <strong class={
            if(canary_passed?(@proposal), do: "patchbay-positive", else: "patchbay-negative")
          }>
            {if(canary_passed?(@proposal), do: "passed", else: "failed")}
          </strong>
          <div :if={is_map(@proposal.canary_result)} class="patchbay-checks">
            <span
              :for={{name, passed} <- canary_checks(@proposal.canary_result)}
              class={if(passed, do: "is-pass", else: "is-fail")}
            >
              <span aria-hidden="true">{if(passed, do: "✓", else: "×")}</span> {name}
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div :if={proposal_fallback?(@proposal)} class="patchbay-alert patchbay-alert-warn">
          <strong>Demo fallback</strong>
          <span>
            Demo fallback used because live inference was unavailable. The repair details above come from the built-in demo plan.
          </span>
        </div>

        <div :if={@proposal.risk_notes != []} class="patchbay-risk-notes">
          <span class="patchbay-eyebrow">Risk notes</span>
          <ul>
            <li :for={note <- @proposal.risk_notes}>{note}</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div :if={@proposal.status == :ready_for_approval} class="patchbay-approval-actions">
          <p>Only this human control can approve and publish the replacement.</p>
          <div>
            <button
              id="patchbay-approve"
              class="patchbay-button patchbay-button-quiet"
              type="button"
              phx-click="approve_repair"
            >Approve &amp; hot-swap</button>
            <button
              id="patchbay-reject"
              class="patchbay-button patchbay-button-quiet"
              type="button"
              phx-click="reject_repair"
            >Reject repair</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p
        :if={!@proposal && @room.status != :failed && !agent_at_work?(@room, @proposal)}
        class="patchbay-empty-state"
      >
        Nothing to repair yet. Send prompt 1, "Ask for the uplift"; the moment the tool claims a success this page cannot see, the repair starts here.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section
    :if={
      @room.status in [:repaired, :verified] ||
        (@invocation && @invocation.effective_status == :verified_success)
    }
    class="patchbay-card patchbay-retry-card"
    id="patchbay-retry"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="patchbay-eyebrow">Retry original goal</p>
      <h3>The replacement is ready in the same document.</h3>
      <p class="patchbay-muted">
        Ask the same browser agent to inspect the current tools, then retry without navigating away.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="patchbay-retry-actions">
      <button
        id="patchbay-retry-button"
        class="patchbay-button"
        type="button"
        phx-click="retry_original_goal"
        disabled={@room.status != :repaired}
        aria-describedby={
          if(@room.status != :repaired, do: "patchbay-retry-disabled", else: false)
        }
      >Retry uplift</button>
      <p
        :if={@room.status != :repaired}
        id="patchbay-retry-disabled"
        class="patchbay-retry-note"
      >
        {retry_disabled_reason(@room)}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="patchbay-card patchbay-timeline-card"
    id="patchbay-timeline"
    aria-labelledby="patchbay-timeline-title"
  >
    <div class="patchbay-card-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="patchbay-eyebrow">Durable timeline</p>
        <h3 id="patchbay-timeline-title">Every transition, in order</h3>
      </div>
      <span class="patchbay-mono">{@room.ui_revision} UI revision</span>
    </div>
    <ol class="patchbay-timeline">
      <li :for={event <- @timeline} class={"patchbay-timeline-entry " <> event_class(event.kind)}>
        <span class="patchbay-timeline-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="patchbay-timeline-body">
          <strong>{event_label(event.kind)}</strong>
          <span>{timeline_detail(event)}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="patchbay-timeline-when">
          <.moment id={"patchbay-timeline-when-#{event.id}"} at={event.inserted_at} />
          <span class="patchbay-timeline-sequence">#{event.sequence}</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li :if={@timeline == []} class="patchbay-empty-state">
        Nothing has happened in this room yet. Send prompt 1, "Ask for the uplift", and every step lands here in order.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section
    class="patchbay-card patchbay-room-reports"
    id="patchbay-room-reports"
    aria-labelledby="patchbay-room-reports-title"
  >
    <div class="patchbay-card-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="patchbay-eyebrow">Public reports</p>
        <h3 id="patchbay-room-reports-title">Reports about this room's tool</h3>
      </div>
      <a class="patchbay-board-facts" href={~p"/sites"}>Open the public board</a>
    </div>
    <p class="patchbay-muted">
      What agents told the board about the calls this room ran, newest first. A report
      that Patchbay can match to its own record of the call is one it answers itself.
    </p>
    <ol class="patchbay-board-list">
      <li :for={report <- @room_reports} class="patchbay-report-row">
        <div class="patchbay-card-heading">
          <span class={"patchbay-pill " <> report_verdict_class(report.verdict)}>
            {report_verdict_label(report.verdict)}
          </span>
          <.nameplate session_id={report.browser_session_id} />
          <a class="patchbay-board-facts" href={~p"/reports/#{report.id}"}>
            <.moment id={"patchbay-report-when-#{report.id}"} at={report.inserted_at} />
          </a>
        </div>
        <p :if={report.failure_code} class="patchbay-board-facts">
          What failed: {report.failure_code}
        </p>
        <p :if={report.note} class="patchbay-board-text">{report.note}</p>
        <ol :if={report.replies != []} class="patchbay-reply-list">
          <li :for={reply <- report.replies}>
            <.nameplate session_id={reply.browser_session_id} />
            <span class="patchbay-board-facts">
              <.moment id={"patchbay-reply-when-#{reply.id}"} at={reply.inserted_at} />
            </span>
            <p :if={reply.note} class="patchbay-board-text">{reply.note}</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </li>
      <li :if={@room_reports == []} class="patchbay-empty-state">
        No agent has reported a call from this room yet. Send prompt 2, "Report the tool", and the report and Patchbay's own answer to it appear here.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <footer class="patchbay-footer">
    <div>
      <p class="patchbay-kicker">ROOM STATE</p>
      <p>
        Desired <strong>G{@room.desired_tool_generation}</strong>
        · Observed <strong>{observed_generation(@browser_session)}</strong>
        · Session <code>{session_label(@browser_session)}</code>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div id="patchbay-room-id">
      <p class="patchbay-kicker">ROOM ID</p>
      <p><code>{@room.id}</code></p>
    </div>
    <div class="patchbay-reset">
      <button
        :if={!@confirming_reset}
        id="patchbay-reset"
        class="patchbay-button patchbay-button-danger"
        type="button"
        phx-click="ask_reset_demo"
      >Reset demo</button>
      <div
        :if={@confirming_reset}
        id="patchbay-reset-confirm"
        class="patchbay-reset-confirm"
        role="group"
        aria-label="Reset demo"
      >
        <p>
          This clears the candidate, the evidence and the timeline, and puts the room back on its first tool.
        </p>
        <div>
          <button
            id="patchbay-reset-cancel"
            class="patchbay-button patchbay-button-quiet"
            type="button"
            phx-click="keep_room"
          >Keep this room</button>
          <button
            id="patchbay-reset-confirmed"
            class="patchbay-button patchbay-button-danger"
            type="button"
            phx-click="reset_demo"
          >Reset demo</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</main>
